[{:round 1, :record {:tests "Independent checks: (1) production equals 80*2=160 verifying tier-one-only rule; (2) rush equals 0 verifying standard-service branch; (3) discount equals 0 verifying nonmember branch; (4) subtotal equals 160+25=185 verifying setup-fee addition; (5) delivery equals 12 verifying 185<250 threshold; (6) tax equals 197*0.08=15.76 verifying tax-on-subtotal-plus-delivery; (7) total equals 212.76 verifying final sum and rounding. These check each rule independently rather than repeating the same computation.", :branches "quantity vs tier boundaries (80 < 100 so all tier-one); rush? false so no rush charge; member? false so no discount; subtotal 185 < 250 so delivery charged", :rules "Progressive tiers: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, rest at $1.30. Rush adds 20% of production. Members get 10% of (production+rush) as discount capped at discount-cap; nonmembers get 0. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery fee $12 waived if subtotal-after-setup >= 250. Tax 8% on (subtotal+delivery). Round final total to cents half-up.", :operators "struct/slot for building and reading quote; + - * / for arithmetic; select for conditional branches (rush, member, delivery threshold); min/max for tier clamping and discount cap; round-money for final rounding; str for text output; network/define for constructing the pricing callable; pricing compound exposes numeric constants but is not a callable that computes a full quote", :outputs "A quote-1 struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total fields, a text reply to user-output-1, and a boolean test result to self-check-1", :operator "construct a network named compute-quote-1 that reads order-1 fields and pricing constants, computes the full breakdown, and writes into quote-1", :units "currency in dollars, copies as integers", :unknowns "none", :facts "quantity-1=80, rush-1=false, member-1=false, discount-cap-1=40, tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.6