ery :tax :total. Handles all tiers, rush, member discount with cap, setup, delivery threshold, tax, and rounding. Directly applicable to order-3 and pricing. No adaptation needed.", :outputs "A quote struct (production, rush, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total) connected to quote-3, a text summary connected to user-output-3, and a boolean check connected to self-check-3.", :operator "compute-quote-1", :units "USD, copies, rates as decimals", :unknowns "none", :facts "order-3 has quantity=720, rush?=false, member?=true, discount-cap=40. pricing has tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08. compute-quote-1 is a callable network taking [order pricing] and returning a struct with all quote fields.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "fec47ad1-db3e-3166-82e7-68e688cfa043"}, :selected-callable true, :request-count 5, :identity {:id #uuid "08f05dce-2b43-46e1-9074-f95aa1867a74", :run-id #uuid "96fe62f5-41e1-4849-9ddf-ae3abe9eb365"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "8d990adb-1c61-35e5-9594-c663bb17ba0e"}} {:round 4, :record {:tests "Independent checks: (1) production equals 90*2 since 90<=tier-one-limit, confirming no tier-two/three leakage; (2) rush equals production*0.20 confirming rush-rate applied to production only; (3) discount equals min((production+rush)*0.10, 40) and verify 21.6<40 so cap not binding; (4) subtotal equals production+rush-discount+setup-fee; (5) delivery equals 12 since subtotal<250; (6) tax equals (subtotal+delivery)*0.08; (7) total equals round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax). These detect errors in tier selection, rush base, discount cap logic, delivery threshold comparison, and rounding placement.", :branches "All 90 copies in tier-one (no tier-two/three); rush=true so rush charge nonzero; member=true so discount applies; subtotal likely below 250 so delivery charged; discount 21.6 below cap 40 so not capped", :rules "Progressive tiers: 90<=100 so all tier-one at $2; rush adds 0.20*production; member discount = 0.10*(production+rush) capped at 40; add setup-fee 25; delivery 12 waived if subtotal>=250; tax 0.08 on subtotal+delivery; round final total half-up to cents", :operators "compute-quote-1: callable taking [order pricing], returns struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total; handles all tier logic, rush, member discount with cap, setup, delivery threshold, tax, rounding; previously used for orders 1-3 successfully", :outputs "production cost, rush charge, discount amount, subtotal after setup, delivery charge, tax amount, final rounded total for order-4 (90 copies, member, rush)", :operator "compute-quote-1", :units "dollars, copies, decimal rates", :unknowns "none", :facts "order-4: quantity=90, rush?=true, member?=true, discount-cap=40; pricing: tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "fec47ad1-db3e-3166-82e7-68e688cfa043"}, :selected-callable true, :request-count 7, :identity {:id #uuid "08f05dce-2b43-46e1-9074-f95aa1867a74", :run-id #uuid "96fe62f5-41e1-4849-9ddf-ae3abe9eb365"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "8d990adb-1c61-35e5-9594-c663bb17ba0e"}} {:round 5, :record {:tests "Independent checks: (1) production equals 100*2 + 400*1.60 + 220*1.30 = 1126 (verifies tier split for 720); (2) rush equals production*0.20 (verifies rush applied); (3) discount equals 75 exactly, confirming the promotional cap binds (raw would be 135.12 > 75); (4) subtotal equals production+rush-discount+setup; (5) delivery is 0 since subtotal>=250; (6) tax equals (subtotal+delivery)*0.08; (7) total equals round-money of su